2|//
3|// Four agents were asked how many callers `has` has. The graph told the two graph-armed ones
4|// `CONFIDENCE: 100 callers`. The real answer is 10 call sites in one function, and one of them wrote
5|// back unprompted: *"the headline number the verb prints is still 100 callers, and 100 is wrong by a
6|// factor of 100."*
7|//
8|// ⭐ AND 100 WAS NEVER A COUNT. `EDGE_FETCH_CAP` is 100, so `mapped.length` saturates there. The verb
9|// already KNOWS it saturated — `edgesTruncated` is computed from a deliberate `LIMIT CAP + 1` — and
10|// that flag reaches the trust banner while never reaching the line that prints the number. Computed
11|// and not consumed, the same shape as the unwired claims this repository keeps finding.
12|//
13|// ⛔ `graph_impact` is worse: it uses `LIMIT 100` with no `+ 1`, so it caps SILENTLY and cannot even
14|// detect that it did. A number it reports as a count may be a cap and nothing in the code can tell.
15|//
16|// ⇒ A capped result is a FLOOR. Saying "100" states a fact the query did not establish, and the
17|// caveat that rescued those agents sits below the number rather than on it.
18|import { describe, it, expect, afterEach } from 'vitest';
19|import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
